# Circutor CVM-BDM.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Circutor CVM-BDM — 3-Phase Supply Network Analyzer (Modbus RTU RS-485)
# | 
# | Source: circutor-cvm-bdm-instruction-manual.pdf (section 12.3, pp. 47-51)
# | Protocol: Modbus RTU, FC03/04 read, FC01 relay read, FC05 relay write, 8N1 default
# | Baud: 1200/2400/4800/9600/19200 bps (configurable; default 9600/8N1)
# | All MODBUS addresses are hexadecimal in source; converted to decimal here.
# | All parameters are 32-bit "longs" (2 consecutive registers).
# | Scaling: V×10, current in mA, Hz×10, PF×100, %×10 (THD/flicker/harmonics).
# | Relay coil addresses (FC01 read, FC05 write): relay 1 = 0x0000, relay 2 = 0x0001.
# | Models: CVM-BDM (base), CVM-BDM-C2 (+2 relays), CVM-BDM-C420 (+relay+AO), CVM-BDM-420 (+2 AO).
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Circutor
@model=CVM-BDM
@vendor_website=circutor.com
@description=3-phase supply network analyzer, Modbus RTU RS-485. FC03/04 read. Phase V/I/P/Q/PF per phase + 3-phase totals (s32, V×10/mA/W/var/PF×100) at addr 0-50. Line-to-line voltages at 52-58. Energy (+/-) kWh/kvarh at 62-74. THD+flicker at 106-128. Harmonics 1-15 I+V at 800-978. Relays via FC01/FC05 on -C2/-C420 variants.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/circutor-cvm-bdm.toml; Source: circutor-cvm-bdm-instruction-manual.pdf (section 12.3, pp. 47-51). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
